      'ಈ ದತ್ತಿಗಳನ್ನು ಕರ್ತ್ತಾರ-ಜೀಯರ ಪಾದ ತೊಳೆದು, ನೀರೆರೆದು (ಧಾರಾಪೂರ್ವಕವಾಗಿ) ಕೊಡಲಾಯಿತು. ಕೊನೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಸಾಂಪ್ರದಾಯಿಕ ಶಾಪಾಶಯವಿದೆ: ಈ ಧರ್ಮವನ್ನು ಕಾಪಾಡಿದವರಿಗೆ ಗಂಗೆ, ಕುರುಕ್ಷೇತ್ರ, ವಾರಣಾಸಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಸಾವಿರ ಕಪಿಲೆ ಹಸುಗಳನ್ನು ದಾನ ಮಾಡಿದ ಪುಣ್ಯ; ಅಳಿಸಿದವರಿಗೆ ಆ ಹಸುಗಳನ್ನೂ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರನ್ನೂ ಕೊಂದ ಪಾಪ. “ಸ್ವದತ್ತಾಂ ಪರದತ್ತಾಂ ವಾ…” ಶ್ಲೋಕವು ತಾನು ಕೊಟ್ಟ ಅಥವಾ ಬೇರೆಯವರು ಕೊಟ್ಟ ಭೂಮಿಯನ್ನು ಕಸಿಯುವವನು ಅರವತ್ತು ಸಾವಿರ ವರ್ಷ ಹುಳುವಾಗಿ ಹುಟ್ಟುತ್ತಾನೆ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತದೆ.',
    glossaryTitle: 'ಕೆಲವು ಪದಗಳ ಅರ್ಥ',
    fromDoc: 'ಮೂಲ ದಾಖಲೆಯಿಂದ',
    textTitle: 'ಪೂರ್ಣ ಪಾಠ',
    textIntro:
      'ಮೂಲ ಹಳಗನ್ನಡ ಲಿಪಿಯ ಪಾಠ, ಹೊಸಗನ್ನಡ ಲಿಪಿಯಲ್ಲಿ. ಮೊದಲ ಸಾಲು ಕಲ್ಲಿನ ಮೇಲ್ಭಾಗದಲ್ಲಿ ಬಿಲ್ಲಿನಾಕಾರದಲ್ಲಿ (ಕಮಾನಿನಂತೆ) ಕೆತ್ತಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿದೆ. [ ] ಆವರಣದಲ್ಲಿರುವ ಅಕ್ಷರಗಳು ಸಂಪಾದಕರು ಪೂರೈಸಿದವು.',
    guide: 'ಶಾಸನದ ಭಾಗಗಳು',
    arched: 'ಕಮಾನಿನ ಸಾಲು',
    journeyTitle: 'ಕಲ್ಲಿನ ಪಯಣ',
    journeyBody:
      'ಈ ಕಲ್ಬರಹವು ಮೊದಲು ಮನಕತ್ತೂರಿನ ಕೆರೆಯ ಹಳೆಯ ಕೋಡಿಯ ಬಳಿ ಇತ್ತೆಂದು ತಿಳಿದುಬರುತ್ತದೆ. ನಂತರ ೧೯೬೦ರ ದಶಕದ ಅಂತ್ಯಭಾಗದಲ್ಲಿ ಅಥವಾ ೧೯೭೦ರ ದಶಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಊರಿನ ಜನರು ಇದನ್ನು ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನಕ್ಕೆ ತಂದು ಕಾಪಾಡಿದ್ದಾರೆ. ಈ ಕಲ್ಬರಹವು ಬಹುಶಃ ಹಿಂದೆ ಕೆರೆಯ ಸಮೀಪ ಇದ್ದಿರಬಹುದಾದ ಹಳೆಯ ದೇವಾಲಯವೊಂದಕ್ಕೆ ಸಂಬಂಧಿಸಿರಬಹುದು.',
    sourcesTitle: 'ಆಧಾರ',
    sources: [
      'ಬೆಂಜಮಿನ್ ಲೂಯಿಸ್ ರೈಸ್ (B. L. Rice), ಸಂ. “ಎಪಿಗ್ರಾಫಿಯಾ ಕರ್ನಾಟಿಕಾ, ಸಂಪುಟ ೫ — ಹಾಸನ ಜಿಲ್ಲೆ”. ಈ ಕಲ್ಬರಹದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ತಿರುಳಾದ ಅರಿವನ್ನು (ಮುಖ್ಯ ಮಾಹಿತಿಯನ್ನು) ಇದು ಒದಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.',
      'ಊರಿನ ದಾಖಲೆ: “ಮನಕತ್ತೂರಿನ ಕಲ್ಬರಹ: ಹೊಯ್ಸಳ ಕಾಲದ ಒಂದು ನೋಟ” (೨೦೨೫).',
    ],
    caveat:
      'ಪಾಠವನ್ನು ಊರಿನ ದಾಖಲೆಯಿಂದ ಅಕ್ಷರಶಃ ಪುನರುತ್ಪಾದಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ; ಸಣ್ಣಪುಟ್ಟ ಮುದ್ರಣ ವ್ಯತ್ಯಾಸಗಳಿರಬಹುದು. ತಿದ್ದುಪಡಿಗಳಿದ್ದರೆ ದಯವಿಟ್ಟು ತಿಳಿಸಿ.',
    back: 'ದೇವಾಲಯದ ಪುಟಕ್ಕೆ ಹಿಂತಿರುಗಿ',
  },
  en: {
    title: 'The Manakathuru Inscription',
    description:
      'The Hoysala-period stone inscription of Manakathuru, dated 1101 CE — its history, meaning, full text and the story of the headmen who founded the village.',
    eyebrow: 'Village heritage',
    h1: 'The Manakathuru Inscription',
    sub: 'A glimpse of the Hoysala age',
    notice:
      'This inscribed stone is kept safe at the Sri Kalabhairaveshwara Temple today, but it is not related to this temple’s history — it is a record of Manakathuru village and of other temples of that time.',
    facts: [
      ['Date', 'Śaka 1022 · 1101 CE'],
      ['Dynasty', 'Hoysala — Vishnuvardhana'],
      ['Language & script', 'Old Kannada (Halegannada)'],
      ['Lines', '44'],
      ['Original location', 'Near the old outlet (kodi) of the village tank'],
      ['Published in', 'Epigraphia Carnatica, Vol. 5 (Hassan)'],
    ],
    toc: 'On this page',
    tocItems: [
      ['overview', 'Overview'],
      ['stone', 'The stone'],
      ['king', 'The king’s titles'],
      ['people', 'People in the record'],
      ['date', 'The date'],
      ['grants', 'The grants'],
      ['text', 'Full text'],
      ['journey', 'The stone’s journey'],
      ['sources', 'Sources'],
    ],
    overviewTitle: 'Overview',
    overview: [
      'Dated Śaka 1022 (1101 CE), in the time of the Hoysala king Vishnuvardhana, this inscription opens with a long eulogy of the king’s titles, and then offers priceless insights into the beliefs and the religious and social life of the community at the time.',
      'It records major temple constructions by local leaders, the installation of deities and gifts of land. Above all, it names the people who founded Manakathuru — then called “Managatur”.',
    ],
    stoneTitle: 'The stone',
    stoneIntro:
      'A tall slab with an arched top: a sculpted panel above, and below it rows of Old Kannada letters across the face of the stone. Today it stands on a black stone base within the temple premises.',
    stoneParts: [
      ['Shiva linga', 'At the centre of the panel — the gifts recorded are to Shiva temples.'],
      ['Seated worshipper', 'On the left, a figure seated in worship — perhaps a donor or priest.'],
      ['Cow and calf', 'On the right — a motif often carved on stones recording gifts.'],
      ['Sun and moon', 'Above — the customary sign that the gift should last “as long as the sun and moon”.'],
      ['The arched line', 'The first line of the inscription runs along the rim of the arch, just as the source document notes.'],
    ],
    stoneCare: 'The letters on the lower part of the stone have worn with time. Please help preserve it — avoid touching the stone or applying turmeric, kumkum or oil, which slowly wear the letters away.',
    kingTitle: 'The king’s titles',
    kingIntro:
      'The first part of the record (lines 3–18) praises the Hoysala king Vishnuvardhana with a garland of titles. Some of them:',
    titles: [
      ['Yadukula-kuvalaya-sudhakara', 'The moon to the lotus of the Yadu race'],
      ['Satya-ratnakara', 'An ocean of truth'],
      ['Dvaravatipura-varadhishvara', 'Supreme lord of Dvaravati (Belur / Halebidu)'],
      ['Shaurya-mrigaraja', 'A lion in valour'],
      ['Talakadugonda-ganda', 'The hero who conquered Talakad'],
      ['Vasantikadevi-labdha-varaprasada', 'Blessed with the grace of the goddess Vasantika'],
    ],
    provinces:
      'He is said to rule Gangavadi 96,000, Nolambavadi 32,000 and Hanungal 500, “punishing the wicked and protecting the good”.',
    peopleTitle: 'People in the record',
    peopleIntro: 'After the royal eulogy, the inscription turns to the people of our village.',
    lineWord: 'Line',
    dateTitle: 'The date',
    dateBody: [
      'The inscription is dated Śaka 1022, in the year named Vikrama, on the fifth day of the bright half of Phalguna, a Monday. This corresponds to 5 February 1101 CE — which by calculation fell on a Tuesday.',
      'The record also mentions the year Yuva, which likely corresponds to 1095 CE.',
    ],
    dateParts: [
      ['Śaka 1022', 'Shalivahana Śaka era — add about 78 to get the CE year'],
      ['Vikrama', 'The name of that year in the 60-year samvatsara cycle'],
      ['Phalguna śuddha pañcamī', 'Fifth day of the bright fortnight of Phalguna'],
      ['Somavara', 'Monday, as stated in the record'],
    ],
    dateNoteTitle: 'A note for history readers',
    dateNote:
      'Historians generally date Vishnuvardhana’s reign from about 1108 CE and his capture of Talakad to about 1116. The title Talakadugonda in a record dated 1101 is therefore noteworthy; in such cases scholars discuss whether the record was engraved later or the date read differently. This page gives the date exactly as the inscription states it.',
    grantsTitle: 'The grants',
    grantsIntro:
      'Wet and dry land was given for the deities’ worship (anga-bhoga), bathing (abhisheka), food offerings and perpetual lamps. The plots are located by village landmarks — below the big tank, below the Adalagatta, in front of the temple, by the stream, to the south (tenkana) and west (haduvana) of the village.',
    grants: [
      ['For Chaveshvara', 'Wet land below the big tank and below the Adalagatta; an ox-driven oil press to keep the perpetual lamp burning.'],
      ['For Moolasthana', 'Wet land in front of the temple, black-soil wet land and dry land.'],
      ['For Chikkeshvara', 'Wet land below the big tank and dry land.'],
      ['For the Brahmins of Brahmapuri', 'Wet land and dry land.'],
      ['For Sankimoja', 'Ten kolaga of wet land and a hundred kamba of dry land.'],
      ['For the gaudas', 'Kodangi wet land below the big tank, gavudagatta and dry land.'],
    ],
    grantsReceiver:
      'The gifts were made by washing the feet of Karttara-jiya and pouring water (dhārāpūrvaka). The record closes with the customary blessing and curse: whoever protects this gift earns the merit of giving a thousand kapila cows at the Ganga, Kurukshetra and Varanasi; whoever destroys it incurs the sin of killing those cows and Brahmins. The Sanskrit verse “svadattām paradattām vā…” warns that one who takes away land given by himself or by others is born a worm for sixty thousand years.',
    glossaryTitle: 'Some words explained',
    fromDoc: 'from the source document',
    textTitle: 'Full text',
    textIntro:
      'The original Old Kannada text, rendered in modern Kannada script. The first line is carved in an arch across the top of the stone. Letters in [ ] are supplied by the editor.',
    guide: 'Parts of the inscription',
    arched: 'arched line',
    journeyTitle: 'The stone’s journey',
    journeyBody:
      'The stone is known to have stood near the old outlet (kodi) of the Manakathuru tank. In the late 1960s or the 1970s the villagers brought it to the temple to keep it safe. It may once have belonged to an old temple that stood near the tank.',
    sourcesTitle: 'Sources',
    sources: [
      'B. L. Rice (ed.), Epigraphia Carnatica, Vol. 5 — Hassan District. The core information about this inscription comes from this volume.',
      'Village document: “ಮನಕತ್ತೂರಿನ ಕಲ್ಬರಹ: ಹೊಯ್ಸಳ ಕಾಲದ ಒಂದು ನೋಟ” (The Manakathuru Inscription: A Glimpse of the Hoysala Age), 2025.',
    ],
    caveat:
      'The text is reproduced as given in the village document; small typographic variations are possible. Corrections are welcome.',
    back: 'Back to the temple page',
  },
}[lang];

// Which section each line starts, for the guide markers in the text panel.
const sectionStarts = new Map<number, (typeof sections)[number]>();
for (const s of sections) if (!sectionStarts.has(s.from)) sectionStarts.set(s.from, s);
---

<Base lang={lang} page="inscription" title={c.title} description={c.description} image="images/shasana-relief.jpg">
  <header class="ins-head">
    <div class="wrap head-grid">
      <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">{c.eyebrow}</p>
      <h1>{c.h1}</h1>
      <p class="sub">{c.sub}</p>
      <dl class="facts">
        {
          c.facts.map(([k, v]) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{k}</dt>
              <dd>{v}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="head-stone">
        <Photo lang={lang} id="stone" eager caption={false} ratio="9 / 16" focus="50% 25%" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 22vw, 50vw" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="notice" role="note">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"></circle><path d="M12 7v6M12 16.5v.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg>
      <span>{c.notice}</span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap ins-layout">
    <nav class="toc" aria-label={c.toc}>
      <p class="toc-title">{c.toc}</p>
      <ol>
        {c.tocItems.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="ins-body">
      <section id="overview" class="block">
        <h2>{c.overviewTitle}</h2>
        {c.overview.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
      </section>

      <section id="stone" class="block">
        <h2>{c.stoneTitle}</h2>
        <p>{c.stoneIntro}</p>
        <Photo lang={lang} id="stoneRelief" zoom sizes="(min-width: 1000px) 50rem, 100vw" />
        <dl class="stone-parts">
          {
            c.stoneParts.map(([k, v]) => (
              <div>
                <dt>{k}</dt>
                <dd>{v}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <p class="note">{c.stoneCare}</p>
      </section>

      <section id="king" class="block">
        <h2>{c.kingTitle}</h2>
        <p>{c.kingIntro}</p>
        <ul class="titles">
          {
            c.titles.map(([t, m]) => (
              <li>
                <span class="title-term" lang={lang === 'en' ? 'kn-Latn' : 'kn'}>{t}</span>
                <span class="title-mean">{m}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p>{c.provinces}</p>
      </section>

      <section id="people" class="block">
        <h2>{c.peopleTitle}</h2>
        <p>{c.peopleIntro}</p>
        <div class="people">
          {
            people.map((p) => (
              <article class="person">
                <h3>{p.name[lang]}</h3>
                <p>{p.role[lang]}</p>
                <p class="person-lines">
                  {lang === 'en' && /[–,]/.test(p.lines) ? 'Lines' : c.lineWord} {num(lang, p.lines)}
                </p>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="date" class="block">
        <h2>{c.dateTitle}</h2>
        {c.dateBody.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
        <dl class="date-parts">
          {
            c.dateParts.map(([k, v]) => (
              <div>
                <dt>{k}</dt>
                <dd>{v}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <aside class="note">
          <strong>{c.dateNoteTitle}.</strong>
          {c.dateNote}
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section id="grants" class="block">
        <h2>{c.grantsTitle}</h2>
        <p>{c.grantsIntro}</p>
        <dl class="grants">
          {
            c.grants.map(([k, v]) => (
              <div>
                <dt>{k}</dt>
                <dd>{v}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <p>{c.grantsReceiver}</p>

        <h3 class="gloss-title">{c.glossaryTitle}</h3>
        <dl class="glossary">
          {
            glossary.map((g) => (
              <div>
                <dt>
                  {g.term[lang]}
                  {lang === 'en' && <span class="gloss-kn" lang="kn"> · {g.term.kn}</span>}
                </dt>
                <dd>
                  {g.meaning[lang]}
                  {g.fromDoc && <span class="gloss-src"> ({c.fromDoc})</span>}
                </dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section id="text" class="block">
        <h2>{c.textTitle}</h2>
        <p>{c.textIntro}</p>

        <div class="stone" lang="kn">
          <svg class="arch" viewBox="0 0 800 190" aria-hidden="true">
            <defs>
              <path id="arch-path" d="M 40 180 A 360 160 0 0 1 760 180"></path>
            </defs>
            <text class="arch-text">
              <textPath href="#arch-path" startOffset="50%" text-anchor="middle" textLength="850" lengthAdjust="spacingAndGlyphs">
                {lines[0]}
              </textPath>
            </text>
          </svg>

          <ol class="lines">
            {
              lines.map((line, i) => {
                const n = i + 1;
                const s = sectionStarts.get(n);
                return (
                  <>
                    {s && <li class="line-section" aria-hidden="true"><span>{s.title[lang]}</span></li>}
                    <li class="line" value={n}>
                      <span class="ln">{num('kn', n)}</span>
                      <span class="lt">
                        {line}
                        {n === 1 && <span class="arch-tag" lang={lang}> ({c.arched})</span>}
                      </span>
                    </li>
                  </>
                );
              })
            }
          </ol>
        </div>

        <h3 class="guide-title">{c.guide}</h3>
        <ol class="guide">
          {
            sections.map((s) => (
              <li>
                <span class="guide-range">
                  {lang === 'en' && s.from !== s.to ? 'Lines' : c.lineWord} {num(lang, s.from === s.to ? s.from : `${s.from}–${s.to}`)}
                </span>
                <strong>{s.title[lang]}</strong>
                <span>{s.summary[lang]}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section id="journey" class="block">
        <h2>{c.journeyTitle}</h2>
        <p>{c.journeyBody}</p>
        <ol class="timeline">
          {
            timeline.map((t) => (
              <li>
                <span class="tl-year">{t.year[lang]}</span>
                <span class="tl-text">{t.text[lang]}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section id="sources" class="block">
        <h2>{c.sourcesTitle}</h2>
        <ul class="sources">
          {c.sources.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="caveat">{c.caveat}</p>
        <p><a href={href(lang, 'temple')}>← {c.back}</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .ins-head {
    background:
      radial-gradient(40rem 24rem at 90% 0%, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.07), transparent 70%),
      linear-gradient(165deg, var(--stone), var(--stone-2));
    color: var(--stone-ink);
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem) clamp(4rem, 9vw, 5.5rem);
  }
  .head-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .head-stone {
    max-width: 13rem;
    width: 100%;
    justify-self: center;
    order: -1;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .head-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 16rem;
      gap: 3.5rem;
    }
    .head-stone {
      max-width: none;
      order: 0;
    }
  }
  .stone-parts {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .stone-parts div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.1rem 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .stone-parts div {
      grid-template-columns: 11rem 1fr;
    }
  }
  .ins-head .eyebrow {
    color: var(--stone-accent);
  }
  .ins-head h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.1em;
  }
  .sub {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2.6vw, 1.5rem);
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    margin: 0;
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);
    border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .facts div {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--stone-2) 88%, black);
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
  }
  .facts dt {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .facts {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .facts dd {
    color: var(--stone-ink);
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .notice {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin: -2rem 0 0;
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 5px solid var(--kumkum);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .notice svg {
    flex: none;
    width: 1.5rem;
    height: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--kumkum);
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }

